.SH NAME
sudoconsole-policy-list - List every binary classified by the policy engine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsudoconsole policy list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
list dumps the (binary → category → risk) table used by the
evaluator. Built-in entries ship with sudoconsole; entries added via
[policy.custom] are flagged with builtin=false.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--cache-timeout\fP=0
	sudo cache timeout in seconds (60-3600); overrides config file

.PP
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the TOML config file (default: platform XDG/Application Support location)

.PP
\fB--format\fP=""
	output format: human or json (overrides config file)

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP=""
	log level: silent, error, warn, info, debug (overrides config file)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  sudoconsole policy list
  sudoconsole --format json policy list
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsudoconsole-policy(1)\fP


